GorasivapadDati":[{"id":"aGoraSivapadDati","headword":"अघोरशिवपद्धति","headword_slp1":"aGoraSivapadDati","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Aghoraśivapaddhati\nby Aghoraśivācārya. "},{"t":"cite","s":"BORI. 337","q":"BOR"},{"t":"txt","s":" of Viś i. D. p. 434. Poona 337. Same a. the Kriyākramadyotikā. According to the Śaivabhūṣaṇa, there are 18 Paddhatis by Śaiva writers, one of which is Aghoraśivācārya's. For mss. see under Kriyākramadyotikā."}]}]}],"aGorasivacarya":[{"id":"aGoraSivAcArya","headword":"अघोरशिवाचार्य","headword_slp1":"aGoraSivAcArya","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Aghoraśivācārya\na Śaiva writer; disciple of Vidyākaṇṭha, the disciple of Rāmakaṇṭha, [Page058-b] who was the son of Nārāyaṇakaṇṭha an. disciple of Utpala (Hz. II. Extr. p. 109); wrote the Mṛgendravṛttidīpikā a. the instance of this Guru; Sarvātmaśiva is usually mentioned a. his chief Guru; was born in the Col. country in the Kauṇḍinyagotra; had the title ‘Lakṣadvayādhyāpaka’, teacher of Mīmāṁsā which is called ‘Lakṣadvaya (?)’; see p. 7. English Intro. to the Bṛhatī, Madras Uni. Skt. Ser. III. ii; mentioned sometimes a. Ghoraśiva an. Parameśvara ("},{"t":"cite","s":"MT. 2104","q":"MT"},{"t":"txt","s":") also; known a. Jñānaśiva too ("},{"t":"cite","s":"MD. 5436","q":"MD"},{"t":"txt","s":") (?); mentions in the Kriyākramadyotikā that he wrote it in Śaka 1080, A. "},{"t":"cite","s":"D. 1157","q":"D"},{"t":"txt","s":". See p. 4, Skt. Intro. to the Chidambaram Grantha edn. of 1927 of the Kriyākramadyotikā in part an. p. 6, Intro. Devakottah Śivāgama Siddhānta Paripālana Saṅgha edn. of the Tattvaprakāśa.\nAccording to Trilocanaśivācārya (Prāyaścittasamuccaya, "},{"t":"cite","s":"Hz. 954","q":"Hz"},{"t":"txt","s":"), Aghoraśivācārya was one of the spiritual heads of the seat called Āmardakamaṭha (Hz. II. Extr. p. 80). Sage Āmardaka was one of the disciples of Durvāsas an. the founder of dualistic Śaiva.\nA traditional version of his story is found in a work called Cidambarasāra. See Tamil Preface to the abovementioned edn. of the Kriyākramadyotikā. This preface an. the Skt. Intro. referred to previously give a list of Āghoraśivācārya's works. Works marked with a. asterisk below are refered to by the a. himself in his Ratnatrayollekhinī (See p. 108 of the Devakottah Śivāgama Siddhānta Paripālana [Page059-a. Saṅgha edn.) an. Mṛgendravṛttidīpikā.\n[Aghoraśivapaddhati. Poona 337.\nSame a. Kriyākramadyotikā].\n*--Abhyudaya. nāṭaka.\n[--Āgamāhnika. Auf. C.. I. p. 39a. Same a. Dīkṣāvidhi below; forms part of Kriyākramadyotikā].\n--Āśaucadīpikā (for Śaivas). "},{"t":"cite","s":"MD. 3027","q":"MD"},{"t":"txt","s":". This does not form part of the Kriyākramadyotikā.\n--Āścaryasāra. kāvya.\n*--Kāvyatilaka. (?) See Mṛgendravṛttidīpikā, Vidyāpāda end.\n--Kriyākramadyotikā (K. k. dyota, K. k. jyoti, Nityakriyākrama, Aghoraśivapaddhati). (Many selections from this have been pub. in S. I. under several titles, with text in Grantha an. with or without Tamil Transl.).\n--Tattvatrayanirṇayavyākhyā. Adyar II. p. 175b. Mysore I. p. 542. "},{"t":"cite","s":"TD. 8187","q":"TD"},{"t":"txt","s":".\nEd.. Devakottah Śivāgama Siddhānta Paripālana Saṅgha 1923.\n--Tattvaprakāśikāvṛtti (Śiva ta. pra. v..). Adyar II. p. 175b. "},{"t":"cite","s":"MT. 3914. 4433","q":"MT"},{"t":"txt","s":". Śṛṅgerī Mutt 216 (2). "},{"t":"cite","s":"TD. 8183","q":"TD"},{"t":"txt","s":".\nEd.. same a. that mentioned above.\n--Tattvasaṅgrahalaghuṭīkā. Mysore I. p. 542. Śṛṅgerī Mutt 216 (3) ? "},{"t":"cite","s":"TD. 8188","q":"TD"},{"t":"txt","s":".\nEd.. same a. that mentioned above.\n[--Dīkṣāvidhi. Auf. C.. "},{"t":"cite","s":"III. 1","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":"b (only a part of the Kriyākramadyotikā)].\n--Dviśatikālottaravyākhyā. Trav. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Uni. 4509","q":"Uni"},{"t":"txt","s":".\n--Nādakārikāvṛtti. "},{"t":"cite","s":"L. 1434","q":"L"},{"t":"txt","s":". "},{"t":"cite","s":"TD. 8191","q":"TD"},{"t":"txt","s":".\nEd.. Devakottah Śivāgama Siddhānta Paripālana Saṅgha 1925. [Page059-b]\n--Parārthanityapūjāvidhi (also called Śivālayanityavidhi).\nEd.. Devakottah Śivāgama Siddhānta Paripālana Saṅgha 1930.\nDoes not seem to form part of the Kriyākramadyotikā; the Col. describes it a. a compilation based on the Sakalāgamasārasaṅgraha for which see "},{"t":"cite","s":"MD. 5549","q":"MD"},{"t":"txt","s":". "},{"t":"cite","s":"TD. 15304","q":"TD"},{"t":"txt","s":".\n*--Pāṣaṇḍāpajaya. kāvya.\n*--Bhaktaprakāśa.\n--Bhogakārikāvṛtti. Mysore I. p. 543. "},{"t":"cite","s":"TD. 8190","q":"TD"},{"t":"txt","s":".\nEd.. Devakottah Śivāgama Siddhānta Paripālana Saṅgha 1925.\n--Mṛgendravṛttidīpikā. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Hz. 1105","q":"Hz"},{"t":"txt","s":".\n--Ratnatrayollekhinī (R. T. Uddyota). Mysore I. p. 544.\nEd.. Devakottah Śivāgama Siddhānta Paripālana Saṅgha 1925.\n--Vṛṣotsarjanaprayoga. Adyar. An extract from his Kriyākramadyotikā ?\n--Sarvajñānottaravṛtti. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Hz. 959","q":"Hz"},{"t":"txt","s":". "},{"t":"cite","s":"TD. 6728","q":"TD"},{"t":"txt","s":". Trav. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Uni. 6578","q":"Uni"},{"t":"txt","s":" (fr.).\n*--Sarvavidyeśinī, a. epitome of Mataṅga an. other Āgamas.\n--Siddhāntaśekhara (?) Śṛṅgerī Mutt 216 (4)."}]}]}],"aGorasanharamantra":[{"id":"aGorasaMhAramantra","headword":"अघोरसंहारमन्त्र","headword_slp1":"aGorasaMhAramantra","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Aghorasaṃhāramantra\nAdyar II. p. 230a."}]}]}],"aGorasahasraksarimantra":[{"id":"aGorasahasrAkzarImantra","headword":"अघोरसहस्राक्षरीमन्त्र","headword_slp1":"aGorasahasrAkzarImantra","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Aghorasahasrākṣarīmantra\nGov. Or. Libr. Madras 1. "},{"t":"cite","s":"MD. 5837","q":"MD"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]}]}],"aGorasudarsanamantra":[{"id":"aGorasudarSanamantra","headword":"अघोरसुदर्शनमन्त्र","headword_slp1":"aGorasudarSanamantra","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Aghorasudarśanamantra\n"},{"t":"cite","s":"MD. 5838","q":"MD"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]}]}],"aGorasubrahmaRyamantra":[{"id":"aGorasubrahmaRyamantra","